{"schema_version":"0.2.0","event_id":"68b7387f-f7f3-4030-b452-2d27977a3b69","trial_id":"lae-mm-v1_all_task_pilot_A4_20260726T043403Z__medium_fateh_002__t03","seq":3,"timestamp":"2026-07-26T09:37:52.561625Z","event_type":"message","agent_role":"reasoner","caused_by":["6eead86f-6541-4dbf-84bd-d4e4d8f0907b"],"payload":{"sender":"reasoner","recipient":"chat_manager","route_reason":"tool_return","text":"### Proof Strategy:\n1. **Sylow Theorems**: Use the Sylow theorems to analyze the number of Sylow 7-subgroups in the group \\( G \\). The number of Sylow 7-subgroups must divide 8 (since \\( 56 = 8 \\times 7 \\)) and must be congruent to 1 modulo 7. The only possibilities are 1 or 8.\n   - If there is 1 Sylow 7-subgroup, it is normal, and \\( G \\) is not simple.\n   - If there are 8 Sylow 7-subgroups, consider the action of \\( G \\) on these subgroups by conjugation. The kernel of this action is a normal subgroup of \\( G \\). If the kernel is non-trivial, \\( G \\) is not simple.\n\n2. **Group Action**: Use the fact that the group \\( G \\) acts on the set of Sylow 7-subgroups by conjugation. The kernel of this action is a normal subgroup of \\( G \\). If the kernel is non-trivial, \\( G \\) is not simple.\n\n3. **Normal Subgroup Construction**: If the kernel of the action is trivial, then \\( G \\) embeds into the symmetric group \\( S_8 \\). However, \\( S_8 \\) has order \\( 40320 \\), which is much larger than 56, and this embedding is impossible due to size constraints. Thus, the kernel must be non-trivial, and \\( G \\) is not simple.\n\n### Known Lemmas:\n- `Sylow.exists_subgroup_card_pow_prime`: Existence of a Sylow \\( p \\)-subgroup.\n- `card_sylow_modEq_one`: The number of Sylow \\( p \\)-subgroups is congruent to 1 modulo \\( p \\).\n- `Sylow.card_dvd_index`: The number of Sylow \\( p \\)-subgroups divides the index of the Sylow \\( p \\)-subgroup.\n- `Sylow.mulAction`: The group action on Sylow \\( p \\)-subgroups.\n- `Subgroup.Normal.mk`: Constructor for a normal subgroup.\n\nHANDOFF: engineer","handoff_target":"engineer"},"anchor":null}
